        {
          "group_id_src": "V-251553",
          "group_id": "V-251553",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-251553",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000141",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_title": "Firefox must be configured to block pop-up windows.",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-251553r960963_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-251553r960963",
          "rule_version": "FFOX-00-000009",
          "rule_title": "Firefox must be configured to block pop-up windows.",
          "severity": "medium",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "discussion": "Pop-up windows may be used to launch an attack within a new browser window with altered settings. This setting blocks pop-up windows created while the page is loading.",
          "check_content": "Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar.\n\nIf \"PopupBlocking\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Default\" \"true\", this is a finding.\nIf \"PopupBlocking\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Locked\" \"true\", this is a finding.\n\n\"PopupBlocking\" \"Enabled\" may be used to specify an allowlist of sites where pop-ups are desired, this is optional.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Mozilla_Firefox_2021_VERSION_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "fix_text": "Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Popups\nPolicy Name: Block pop-ups from websites\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nPolicy Name: Do not allow preferences to be changed\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nOptional:\nPolicy Name: Allowed Sites\nPolicy State: Enabled\nClick \"Show...\" and enter a list of websites to be allowlisted.\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n<key>PopupBlocking</key>\n  <dict>\n    <key>Allow</key>\n    <array>\n      <string>http://example.mil</string>\n      <string>http://example.gov</string>\n    </array>\n    <key>Default</key>\n    <true/>\n    <key>Locked</key>\n    <true/>\n  </dict>\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"PopupBlocking\": {\n      \"Allow\": [\"http://example.mil/\",\n                \"http://example.gov/\"],\n      \"Default\": true,\n      \"Locked\": true}",
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000381"
          ],
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "srg_id": "SRG-APP-000141",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
